preConditionHook:
// EL: one pass over bars 0..lookback-1 (current bar INCLUDED, CountIF's
// convention) accumulating close - open on up bars into bullBodySum and
// open - close on down bars into bearBodySum; and
// bullBodySum > dominanceMultiple * bearBodySum on the long side.
//
// Buying pressure by body size rather than bar count -- the body-weighted
// twin of TrendBarCountDominanceInWindow, where one big bull bar can carry the
// window and cannot there. No body-fraction test on the individual bars: the
// sum itself does the weighting, which is what makes it a different rule.
// A tie bar (close == open within the EL tolerance) adds nothing to either
// side.
//
// Summed over price expressions with real history, so a fresh loop -- not the
// WFSafe_ rolling accumulator and not a zero-filled variable mirror -- and
// newest-first, EasyLanguage's Summation order.
//
// Both accumulators are class members and persist across bars, so they are
// reset before the loop; both are computed here rather than in the conditions
// because EasyLanguage does not short-circuit.
bullBodySum = 0.0;
bearBodySum = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)lookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(close[i], open[i])) bullBodySum = bullBodySum + (close[i] - open[i]);
    if (el_lt(close[i], open[i])) bearBodySum = bearBodySum + (open[i] - close[i]);
}
